comments.body:
@elarlang as with all things OWASP and community, you have to understand that people come and go and give their time when they can. Normally this is quicker, but look at what is happening in the world right now. We are in a very ugly period of human history, most are worrying about losing their jobs, or trying to balance childcare and working from home. It's unprecedented pressure so yeah, sometimes the communications are slower than usual. It's not ignorance or ignoring, it's literally 'shit, i need to take care of the kids, ensure the house is clean, do work, worry about not getting fired and so on'

I, for one, truly **appreciate** what you do for the project and indeed so many others do. We aren't ignoring it at all, but sometimes comms will be slow for the above reasons. 

:) no hard feelings here at all, just take into account others time and how they might be struggling.
